  "content": [
    {
      "text": "not take the name of the Lord thy God in vain, Ex. 20:7 (Deut. 5:11; 2 Ne. 26:32; D&C 136:21). hired vain and light persons, Judg. 9:4. for then should ye go after vain things, 1 Sam. 12:21. Why do … the people imagine a vain thing, Ps. 2:1 (Acts 4:25). It is vain for you to rise up early, Ps. 127:2. thine enemies take thy name in vain, Ps. 139:20. he that followeth vain persons is void of understanding, Prov. 12:11. he that followeth after vain persons shall have poverty, Prov. 28:19. Bring no more vain oblations, Isa. 1:13. How long shall thy vain thoughts lodge within thee, Jer. 4:14. Ye have said, It is vain to serve God, Mal. 3:14 (3 Ne. 24:14).",
