    {
      "text": "when ye pray, use not vain repetitions, Matt. 6:7 (3 Ne. 13:7). in vain they do worship me, Matt. 15:9 (Mark 7:7). they … became vain in their imaginations, Rom. 1:21. Lord knoweth the thoughts of the wise, that they are vain, 1 Cor. 3:20. your faith is vain, 1 Cor. 15:17. if righteousness come by the law, then Christ is dead in vain, Gal. 2:21. lest … the tempter have tempted you, and our labour be in vain, 1 Thes. 3:5. some … have turned aside unto vain jangling, 1 Tim. 1:6. avoiding profane and vain babblings, 1 Tim. 6:20 (2 Tim. 2:16). there are many unruly and vain talkers, Titus 1:10. bridleth not his tongue … this man’s religion is vain, James 1:26. vain conversation received by tradition, 1 Pet. 1:18.",
